{"call_id": "3db6b809ef5a48d28d4b903d507fdc35", "success": true, "result_file": "/data/nly/Agent-Aware-Trajectory-Level-Query/benchmark/quickcheck/runs/natural/stockindex/query1/quick-01/results/3db6b809ef5a48d28d4b903d507fdc35.json", "row_count": null, "preview": "{\"submitted\": true, \"answer\": \"The Asia-region stock index with the highest average intraday volatility since 2020 is the Shenzhen Component Index (symbol: 399001.SZ), traded on the Shenzhen Stock Exchange (China, currency CNY).\\n\\nMethod: For each Asian index in index_trade (000001.SS Shanghai, 399001.SZ Shenzhen, HSI Hong Kong, NSEI India, N225 Tokyo/Japan, TWII Taiwan), intraday volatility per day was measured as the daily High-Low range relative to price, averaged over all trading days from 2020-01-01 onward.\\n\\nResults (average daily High-Low range as % of close, since 2020):\\n1. 399001.SZ (Shenzhen Component, China): ~2.02% (2,719 trading days)  <- highest\\n2. 000001.SS (SSE Composite, Shanghai, China): ~1.73%\\n3. NSEI (NIFTY 50, India): ~1.59%\\n4. HSI (Hang Seng, Hong Kong): ~1.38%\\n5. TWII (Taiwan Weighted, Taiwan): ~1.35%\\n6. N225 (Nikkei 225, Japan): ~0.87%\\n\\nThe ranking is robust to the normalization choice (range over close, over open, or over mid-price all give the same ordering).\\n\"}", "truncated": false}
